%C - feed USB keyboard input into a tty

Syntax:
%C [-v] [tty]

   tty   character device that receives the key presses (default /dev/ser10)
   -v    print the raw key usages

Key presses on any USB (HID) keyboard are injected into the input of the
given tty as if they had been typed on it, so a keyboard can drive the shell
of a serial console. US layout, no key repeat. Requires io-hid -d usb.
